From: ad5x <ad5x@localhost>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stm32: N32G455 has 128KiB RAM

The Flashforge AD5X eboard bootloader does not start an application whose
initial stack pointer is 0x20010000 (64KiB RAM): it stays in the
bootloader. Stock firmware for both AD5X boards uses 0x20020000, as does
xblax/klipper's MACH_N32G455xC. Use 128KiB for N32G455 builds.
---
 src/stm32/Kconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/stm32/Kconfig b/src/stm32/Kconfig
index e9aa08791..429538d8c 100644
--- a/src/stm32/Kconfig
+++ b/src/stm32/Kconfig
@@ -257,6 +257,7 @@ config RAM_SIZE
     default 0x9000 if MACH_STM32G07x
     default 0x24000 if MACH_STM32G0Bx
     default 0x20000 if MACH_STM32H7
+    default 0x20000 if MACH_N32G455 # AD5X: as stock; the eboard bootloader checks the stack pointer
     default 0x10000 if MACH_N32G45x
 
 config STACK_SIZE
-- 
2.56.0

